<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    Root Android Lint configuration, applied to every Android module by the
    convention in build.gradle.kts.

    Zero-tolerance for unused resources: any orphaned string, drawable, color,
    layout, or dimen makes `lintDebug` fail (severity=error). This is the real
    Lint UnusedResources analysis — dependency/cross-module aware by design —
    so a string that is referenced anywhere (including across modules via a
    dependency's R class) is never flagged, while a genuinely dead resource
    blocks the build and is reported by the CI script
    scripts/check_resources.py.

    The translation-integrity checks (MissingTranslation, ExtraTranslation) are
    errors too: every locale must be a strict superset/subset of the default
    `values/strings.xml` (the parity script enforces identical key sets, so a
    missing or orphaned translation is a genuine defect, never a locale that
    intentionally falls back). UnusedIds flags view IDs declared with @+id that
    are never referenced — dead markup. All three fail the build and surface in
    the CI lint report.

    Code-quality and string-hygiene checks are errors as well:
    CheckResult (ignoring the return value of a @CheckResult method),
    HardcodedText (user-visible text hardcoded in layouts or Compose instead of
    a string resource) and TypographyDashes (literal dash characters in string
    resources that must use \u2013/\u2014 escapes). Like the resource checks,
    each is guarded in scripts/check_resources.py so a future relaxation fails
    the gate before a lint run.

    Deliberate non-zero-tolerance relaxations, kept here (not in per-module
    lint.xml files) so every module inherits the exact same config and no
    module file can ever carry a hidden ignore-list:
    - ProtectedPermissions: the manifest declares signature/privileged
      permissions intentionally (custom-ROM system-app integration, see
      core/rom-integration/privapp-permissions-nexaflow.xml); they are granted
      only in priv-app and the app degrades gracefully without them.
    - GradleDependency / NewerVersionAvailable: dependency versions are pinned
      in gradle/libs.versions.toml deliberately for reproducible builds;
      "newer version available" hints are noise.
-->
<lint>
    <issue id="UnusedResources" severity="error" />
    <issue id="MissingTranslation" severity="error" />
    <issue id="ExtraTranslation" severity="error" />
    <issue id="UnusedIds" severity="error" />
    <issue id="CheckResult" severity="error" />
    <issue id="HardcodedText" severity="error" />
    <issue id="TypographyDashes" severity="error" />

    <issue id="ProtectedPermissions" severity="ignore" />
    <issue id="GradleDependency" severity="ignore" />
    <issue id="NewerVersionAvailable" severity="ignore" />
</lint>
